      <div type="clause" n="22.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 22.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 22.1" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="561" ed="#liebermann"/>Sepe etiam ex i[nsc]icia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.4"/> placitancium cause transeunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.b"/> in ius aliorum: exaggeracione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.c"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.5"/> rerum — ut qui nominant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.6"/> et promittunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.7"/> ‘grithbreche’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.8"/> uel ‘hamsocnam’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.9"/> uel eorum aliquid quod socnam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.10"/> et sacam eorum excedit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.11"/>, ipsa nocendi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.12"/> cupiditate<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.13"/> prepositi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.14"/>, dum ad witam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.15"/> castigacius posset inflecti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.16"/> —; difforciacione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.17"/> recti; miscrauacione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.18"/>; presumptis accusacionibus; tarditate — ut qui in prefectura uel qualibet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.19"/> potestate constitutus, sepe differt exigere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.d"/>, dum licet, quod sepe cum labore frustraque<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.20"/> prosequitur destitutus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.e"/> —; transeunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.21"/> etiam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.22"/> in mislocutione<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.23"/> — miskenninge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.24"/> —, que magis inhorruit in Londonia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.f"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 561 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 9, 4 <hi rend="italic">f. Verf. zählt sechs Gründe auf für Übergang der Processe an andere Instanz</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 9, 4 f. The author lists six reasons for the transfer of cases to another court</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">durch Gebrauch eines übertreibenden Ausdrucks für den Thatbestand — z. B. wenn Kläger ‘G.’ oder ‘H.’ [<hi rend="italic">dem Richter; vgl.</hi> 80, 9] angeben und [zu erweisen ihm] geloben [<hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 24, 2] oder derlei, was die Jurisdictions-Competenz der Gerichtsherren übersteigt [<hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 24, 4], gerade durch die Sportelgier des Gerichtsvogts, obwohl es bei Mässigung auf ‘Strafgeld’ eingeschränkt werden könnte [das dem Immunitätsherrn zustände]. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. über</hi> exaggeratio: Quadr. Ded. 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">by using an exaggerated expression for the facts of the case — e.g. when plaintiffs declare ‘G.’ or ‘H.’ [to the judge; cf. 80, 9] and pledge themselves [to prove it] [cf. 24, 2], or the like, which exceeds the jurisdictional competence of the lords of the court [cf. 24, 4], precisely through the court reeve's greed for fees, although with moderation it could be restricted to a ‘fine’ [which would be due to the lord of the immunity]. On exaggeratio cf. Quadr. Ded. 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[aus der Habe des Beklagten] beizutreiben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">to be exacted [from the defendant's property]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">der geschädigte [Kläger]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the injured [plaintiff]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geschrieben vor Hn Lond</hi> 8, <hi rend="italic">o. S.</hi> 525</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written before Hn Lond 8, above p. 525</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iusti. <hi rend="italic">Hss. Edd.; verb. aus</hi> 9, 4<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iusti. MSS Edd.; corrected from 9, 4<hi rend="italic">a</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ex aggregacione <hi rend="italic">K Co Or Gi Sl Tw</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ex aggregacione K Co Or Gi Sl Tw</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ut <hi rend="italic">fügt ein, aber vom Corr. unterpunctirt Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sc inserts ut, but it is underdotted by the corrector</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">permittunt <hi rend="italic">Gi Sl Tw</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">permittunt Gi Sl Tw</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gritb. <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> grindeb. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gritb. Sc; grindeb. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-na <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> -okn. <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-na Sc; -okn. Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">socham et sacham <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">socham et sacham Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">accedit <hi rend="italic">Tw</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">accedit Tw</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nosc. <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg;</hi> nodi <hi rend="italic">Wi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">nosc. Sc Hg; nodi Wi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tem <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tem Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-posii, <hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> -stera <hi rend="italic">mit Vergessung eines Striches Sc;</hi> -post'i <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> preposteri <hi rend="italic">Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-posii, altered to -stera with one stroke forgotten Sc; -post'i K; preposteri Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wyt. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wyt. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inflicti <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inflicti Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> -nem <hi rend="italic">Sc;</hi> defo. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from -nem Sc; defo. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-em <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-em Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tarditate <hi rend="italic">fügt ein, aber vom Corr. unterpunctirt Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tarditate inserted, but dotted for deletion by the corrector, Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">frustra et <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">frustra et Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nsse. <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nsse. Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">autem <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">autem Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">loc. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> id est <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Wi</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">loc. Lond; id est added by Wi</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.24" n="24" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">561</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nyng <hi rend="italic">Co;</hi> myskennyng' <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nyng Co; myskennyng' Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Instanzenzug 6—10; Kronprozess 6—<hi rend="italic">iusticia</hi>{4}—<hi rend="italic">ex aggregacione</hi>{5}—<hi rend="italic">permittunt</hi>{7} <hi rend="italic">grindeb. uel hamsocam</hi>—<hi rend="italic">socam</hi>{10} <hi rend="italic">et sacham</hi>—<hi rend="italic">preposteri</hi>{14}—<hi rend="italic">frustra et</hi>{20} <hi rend="italic">p. d. transseunt c. m</hi>. (ohne <hi rend="italic">in</hi>) <hi rend="italic">miskennige</hi> Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Instanzenzug 6—10; Kronprozess 6—<hi rend="italic">iusticia</hi>{4}—<hi rend="italic">ex aggregacione</hi>{5}—<hi rend="italic">permittunt</hi>{7} <hi rend="italic">grindeb. uel hamsocam</hi>—<hi rend="italic">socam</hi>{10} <hi rend="italic">et sacham</hi>—<hi rend="italic">preposteri</hi>{14}—<hi rend="italic">frustra et</hi>{20} <hi rend="italic">p. d. transseunt c. m</hi>. (without <hi rend="italic">in</hi>) <hi rend="italic">miskennige</hi> Rs</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_22-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">319</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht ‘ungerechte’ (Ducange, Schmid) oder ‘zu späte Klage, der andere zuvorkam’ (Wilkins <hi rend="italic">Leges Agsax</hi>. 395), sondern Missesprechen; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5. a. Es besteht damals in London, wurde aber bald nách Hn abgeschafft durch Hn Lond 8</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not ‘unjust’ (Ducange, Schmid) or ‘a suit brought too late, which another forestalled’ (Wilkins <hi rend="italic">Leges Agsax</hi>. 395), but mis-speaking; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5. a. It existed in London at that time, but was abolished soon <hi rend="italic">after</hi> Hn by Hn Lond 8</seg></note>
